Make the legacy (non-WebRender) EGL path bind the GLES client API on
drivers that expose no desktop-OpenGL API.

GLContextEGLFactory::Create() already retries with aUseGles=true when the
desktop-GL attempt fails, but CreateImpl() set REQUIRE_COMPAT_PROFILE purely
on !aWebRender, so the GLES retry also received that flag. CreateGLContext()
turns REQUIRE_COMPAT_PROFILE into EGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_PROFILE_MASK and
EGL_CONTEXT_OPENGL_COMPATIBILITY_PROFILE_BIT, which are desktop-GL-only and
are rejected with EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE when a GLES context is requested, so the
existing fallback could never succeed.

Gate the flag on !aUseGles so the compatibility profile is requested only for
the desktop-GL attempt. Nothing else changes: the GLES path already requests
EGL_OPENGL_ES2_BIT in CreateConfig() and EGL_CONTEXT_MAJOR_VERSION 2 here.

--- a/gfx/gl/GLContextProviderEGL.cpp
+++ b/gfx/gl/GLContextProviderEGL.cpp
@@ -289,7 +289,7 @@ already_AddRefed<GLContextEGL> GLContextEGLFactory::CreateImpl(
   if (aWebRender && aUseGles) {
     flags |= CreateContextFlags::PREFER_ES3;
   }
-  if (!aWebRender) {
+  if (!aWebRender && !aUseGles) {
     flags |= CreateContextFlags::REQUIRE_COMPAT_PROFILE;
   }

